.TH AUTODND 1 "2026" "autodnd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
autodnd \- schedule the GNOME Do Not Disturb state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B autodnd
[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR | \fB\-\-once\fR]
.br
.B autodnd
\fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B autodnd
is a small daemon that toggles the GNOME notifications
.I show-banners
setting on a weekly schedule, effectively turning Do Not Disturb on and off
at user-defined times. Configuration is a plain-text file at
.IR ~/.config/autodnd/config.txt .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Log at DEBUG level. Without this flag,
.B autodnd
logs at INFO level (every state transition, plus reload events).
.TP
.B \-\-check
Parse the config file, print every expanded occurrence with start and end
timestamps, and exit. Exit status is 2 on a malformed config; the offending
line number is included in the error message.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the desired Do Not Disturb state for the current minute and the time
of the next scheduled transition, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single iteration of the scheduler — apply the desired state for the
current minute via
.BR gsettings (1)
\(em and exit. Suitable for cron.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Each non-comment line is one event:
.PP
.RS
\fI<days>\fR \fI<start\-time>\fR \fI<end\-time>\fR
.RE
.PP
.I days
is one or more of:
.IP \(bu 2
numbers 0\-6, where 0 is Monday and 6 is Sunday;
.IP \(bu
weekday names
.RB ( mon ", " tue ", " wed ", " thu ", " fri ", " sat ", " sun );
.IP \(bu
ranges
.RB ( "0\-4" ", " "mon\-fri" );
.IP \(bu
aliases
.RB ( weekdays ", " weekends ", " all );
.IP \(bu
any of the above comma-mixed, e.g.\&
.BR "weekdays,sat" .
.PP
Times are
.BR HH:MM ,
24-hour. When
.I end-time
is earlier than
.IR start-time ,
the event spans midnight. Lines starting with
.B #
(or anything after a
.B #
on a line) are comments.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the config file without restarting. Useful with
.IR "systemctl --user reload autodnd" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/autodnd/config.txt
Schedule configuration. Created on first run if missing.
.TP
.I /usr/share/autodnd/config-sample.txt
Annotated sample config installed by the package.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/autodnd.service
Systemd user unit installed by the package.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate the config and list every expanded occurrence:
.PP
.RS
.B autodnd \-\-check
.RE
.PP
Run the scheduler from cron once a minute instead of as a daemon:
.PP
.RS
.B * * * * *   /usr/bin/autodnd \-\-once
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andreas Pachler <apachler@paan-systems.com>
